---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';const base='/equipment/08-01/',uc='https://cnm2.ucdavis.edu/equipment/west-bond-7700e-ball-bonder',ds='https://www.artisantg.com/info/west_bond_7400e_7600e__7700e_datasheet.pdf';
---
<Layout pageTitle="West-Bond 7700E manual ball bonder" description="Place a virtual ball-to-stitch interconnect and verify the graph of an inert two-net coupon." wide={true}><article class="equipment" id="bondbench"><nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/08-01/">← Equipment 08-01</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Register</a><a href="#bond-evidence">References</a></nav><header class="eq-mast"><p class="eq-meta">08-01 / CHIP PACKAGING</p><h2>One wire, two different ends</h2><p class="eq-lede">Place a ball on die pad D_A, then place the stitch on carrier pad C_A. The new loop should connect A without changing either B pad. Try landing off the edge or using the wrong net to see what the verifier reports.</p></header>
<div class="b-cols"><section><h3>West-Bond 7700E station</h3><canvas id="bond-model" aria-label="Orbitable ball bonder and chip-carrier coupon"></canvas><p id="bond-viewstatus" role="status">Loading metric GLB…</p><button id="bond-front">Whole station / reset view</button><button id="bond-tool">Bond head</button><button id="bond-coupon">Coupon microscope view</button><p>Click the manipulator ball to commit the selected endpoint, or use the control beside the viewer. In the microscope view, the pads are directly pickable. The capillary tip follows the selected endpoint during placement.</p></section>
<section><h3>Two-net coupon</h3><p id="bond-phase"></p><div class="b-pads">{[['D_A','Die A'],['D_B','Die B'],['C_A','Carrier A'],['C_B','Carrier B']].map(([k,l])=><button data-bond-pad={k}>{l} · {k}</button>)}</div><div class="b-settings"><label>Transverse touchdown offset, µm<input type="number" id="bond-shift" min="-100" max="100" step="any" value="0"/></label><label>Loop control lift, mm<input type="number" id="bond-apex" min=".12" max=".60" step="any" value=".35"/></label></div><button id="bond-place">Place ball</button><button id="bond-cancel">Cancel unfinished loop</button><button id="bond-reset">Reset coupon</button><p id="bond-status" role="status"></p></section></div>
<section><h3>Assembly and net isolation</h3><div class="b-cols"><canvas id="bond-preview" width="590" height="275" aria-label="Idealized side profile of the first wire loop"></canvas><div><p id="bond-edges"></p><p id="bond-test" role="status"></p><button id="bond-export">Download assembly JSON</button><p><a href={base+'example-assembly.json'}>Example assembly</a>. The file supplies sample/revision IDs, pad IDs and intended nets, ordered endpoints, centerline and connected components, all in a defined metric frame.</p></div></div></section>
<section id="bond-evidence"><h3>What the first pass models</h3><p>West-Bond 7700E single ball-to-stitch configuration, with binocular microscope and workholder as photographed by <a href={uc}>UC Davis CNM2</a>. The enclosure, controls and accessory geometry are inferred from that view, not factory CAD. The 15.875 mm capillary length is the shorter option in the <a href={ds+'#page=3'}>West-Bond E-series datasheet, PDF p. 3</a>; the stated 14.2875 mm vertical and 15.875 mm horizontal travel bound the synthetic fixture. The vendor offers different microscopes and workholders; rear connectors and spool path here are illustrative.</p>
<div class="b-cols"><figure><img src={base+'station.webp'} alt="Original 7700E station view"/><figcaption>Original station geometry compared with the <a href={uc}>UC Davis 7700E photograph</a>; the linked source documents the installed controls, eyepieces, arm and specimen platform.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src={base+'coupon.webp'} alt="Original chip carrier with finished curved interconnect"/><figcaption>Original microscope view of a designed demonstration coupon, not a photograph. The 25.4 µm wire and approximate 75 µm ball diameter follow the UC Davis configuration. Stitch footprint is assumed (30 × 50 µm).</figcaption></figure></div>
<p>The entire touchdown footprint must fall within its pad. The completed loop is a cubic Bézier path between measured virtual endpoints. Graph traversal checks actual wire connections, separate from intended net IDs. A wrong-net stitch creates a marked short in the virtual assembly, not a hidden correction. This does not model thermosonic force, metallurgy, pull-test strength or 3D routing collisions; no physical process recipe is given.</p>
<table><thead><tr><th>Register check</th><th>Expected</th><th>Actual</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Endpoint order</td><td>D_A ball, C_A stitch</td><td>D_A → C_A</td></tr><tr><td>Neighbor net</td><td>D_B and C_B both isolated</td><td>Both singleton components</td></tr><tr><td>100 µm pad / 75 µm ball</td><td>12.500 µm offset fits; 12.501 µm fails</td><td>Pass / rejected</td></tr><tr><td>Wrong carrier</td><td>D_A → C_B identified as a short</td><td>WIRE-1 marked short</td></tr></tbody></table><p><a href={base+'build-model.py'}>Editable Blender source</a> · <a href={base+'west-bond-7700e.glb'}>Metric GLB</a> · <a href={base+'interconnect.mjs'}>Solver and state actions</a> · <a href={base+'vr.json'}>VR hit bounds, pivot and asset budget</a>. No Quest check is claimed.</p></section></article></Layout>
<script>import '../../../../lib/equipment/08-01/client.mjs';</script>
<style is:global>#bondbench .b-cols{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.15fr) minmax(0,1fr);gap:1rem}#bondbench section{padding:1rem;border:1px solid var(--border);margin:1rem 0;min-width:0}#bondbench :is(input,button){font:inherit;color:inherit;background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--border);padding:.45rem;max-width:100%;box-sizing:border-box}#bondbench button{margin:.35rem .25rem .2rem 0;cursor:pointer}#bondbench button:disabled{opacity:.5}#bondbench button[aria-pressed=true],#bondbench button:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #b28d5e}#bondbench .b-pads,#bondbench .b-settings{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.45rem}#bondbench .b-settings label{display:grid;gap:.25rem;min-width:0}#bondbench .b-settings input{width:100%;min-width:0}#bond-model{display:block;width:100%;height:350px;touch-action:none}#bond-preview{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;background:#162229}#bondbench figure{margin:.5rem 0}#bondbench figure img{width:100%}#bondbench table{font-size:.9rem;border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;text-align:left}#bondbench td,#bondbench th{border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);padding:.35rem}@media(max-width:780px){#bondbench .b-cols{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr)}#bond-model{height:280px}}</style>
